  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening National Policing Capacity in the Republic of Moldova</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the proposed intervention is to enhance General Inspectorate of Police&#x2019;s (GIP) capacity to mitigate the impacts of the full-scale Russia-Ukraine war on the public order and safety in the Republic of Moldova, while continuing to develop a rights-based, gender-sensitive, and inclusive migration management framework. This will be done through 2 different outcomes, aiming to strengthen GIP&#x2019;s community engagement, policing (CEP), trust, and cooperation while enhancing intelligence-led policing measures and the ability of national authorities to respond to cross-border crime. IOM will provide equipment and technical support to the GIP while organizing communication and capacity-building initiatives on CEP for law enforcement authorities and communities, focusing particularly on those hosting a significant number of refuges, aiming to implement a holistic approach to ensure the effective protection of fundamental rights and a better quality of life. Additionally, IOM will work to enhance national authorities&apos; Intelligence-Led Policing (ILP) approaches through the development of risk analysis capacities and cooperation modalities, including with and within the recently established National Center for Integrated Coordination of Public Order Actions (NICPOA), as well as the procurement and delivery of specialised equipment.</narrative>
  </description>
